---
import './style.css'
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8">
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
	<title>Taxi.js — Fox</title>
	<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
</head>
<body>
	<div data-taxi>
		<div data-taxi-view>
			<main class="detail">
				<a class="back-link" href="/view-transitions-demo/gallery">← Back to gallery</a>

				<div class="photo photo-1" style="view-transition-name: photo-1">🦊</div>

				<h1>Fox</h1>
				<p>Only this photo element carries <code>view-transition-name: photo-1</code>, matching the same name on the gallery card. Because the names match, the browser morphs the shared element between its old position/size and its new one instead of just cross-fading it.</p>
				<p>The heading and this text have no <code>view-transition-name</code>, so they use the default root transition (a simple cross-fade) - proving a single element can be singled out for its own animation.</p>
			</main>
		</div>
	</div>

	<script src="../../js/view-transitions-demo.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
